From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: clear error pointers on phylink setup failure

ppe_port_phylink_setup() assigns the result of ipq_pcs_get() and
phylink_create() directly to ppe_port->pcs and ppe_port->phylink.  If
either call fails, the ERR_PTR value is left in the structure.

ppe_port_phylink_destroy() only checks these members for NULL, so any
later call on the same port would hand the error pointer to
ipq_pcs_put(), phylink_disconnect_phy() and phylink_destroy().

Set both members to NULL when the calls fail.  The success path is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jackie Han <jackie.han@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -1117,7 +1117,9 @@ int ppe_port_phylink_setup(struct ppe_port *ppe_port, struct net_device *netdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(ppe_port->pcs)) {
 		dev_err(ppe_dev->dev, "PPE port %d failed to create PCS\n",
 			ppe_port->port_id);
-		return PTR_ERR(ppe_port->pcs);
+		ret = PTR_ERR(ppe_port->pcs);
+		ppe_port->pcs = NULL;
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	/* Port phylink capability */
@@ -1140,6 +1142,7 @@ int ppe_port_phylink_setup(struct ppe_port *ppe_port, struct net_device *netdev)
 		dev_err(ppe_dev->dev, "PPE port %d failed to create phylink\n",
 			ppe_port->port_id);
 		ret = PTR_ERR(ppe_port->phylink);
+		ppe_port->phylink = NULL;
 		goto err_free_pcs;
 	}
 
